  year={2021},
  publisher={IEEE},
  comments={The Combinatorial BLAS library implements key computational primitives for rapid development of combinatorial algorithms in distributed-memory systems. 
  OBSERVATIONS:
  (1) Exascale computers are going to be based on either accelerators or multi-core CPUs.
  (2) CombBLAS introduces accelerator sup- port for several key operations to address the shift in super- computer architectures towards exascale.
  PROBLEMS:
  (1) Communication is the primary bottleneck in scaling data-intensive applications to exascale.
  (2) a flat MPI model is now known to be unscalable due to increased communication bottlenecks in Network Interface Card (NIC)
  (3) popular sparse data structures such as Compressed Sparse Columns (CSC) become wasteful as local matrices become hypersparse due to 2D or 3D decomposition on large numbers of partitions.
  (4) Use of accelerators introduces an overhead for copying from the hose to the accelerator; so the gain from the accelerator must outweigh the cost of copying it across
  (5) I/O has increasingly become a bottleneck on exascale systems. The graph community does not have a commonly accepted binary exchange format.
